@Lalatendu Mohanty Similar to the rpms.lock.yaml hermetic approach, wheel dependencies are intentionally locked/hardcoded in requirements.txt to specific artifacts (We autogen from pyproject.toml). This is by design to ensure reproducibility. The reason you see around 90 wheel files is that our repository contains multiple pyproject.toml files, each corresponding to a different image. In contrast, we only maintain a single rpm.in.yaml that covers all images.
We at Notebook regenerate the requirements.txt file periodically because we’re uncertain when a new wheel becomes available for consumption. I’d like the notifications when new indices are released, enabling us to manage our GHA flow more effectively and regenerate the lock files accordingly.

For Hermeto/Konflux prefetching in general, the requirements.txt/pylock.yaml files should be treated as static snapshots of the moment in time.

